            {
              "code": "discrimination",
              "params": {
                "ratio": "1.6"
              },
              "text": "Each breaker is rated at least 1.6 x the largest breaker after it, so they discriminate on overload. On short circuit, miniature breakers discriminate only up to the upstream breaker's instantaneous trip (about 5 x In for curve C); where total selectivity is required, confirm it from the manufacturer's selectivity tables."
